From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a webview's page opens a real window

A page's `window.open()` and `target="_blank"` returned null from a
<webview> guest: WebContentsImpl::CreateNewWindow CHECKs that a guest
has a guest SiteInstance, so WebViewGuest overrode creation and opened
a browser window at the address. The page lost its window handle, the
opener, the target name and a form's POST body.

A guest SiteInstance needs a partition of its own, which would log the
user out of every site, so Domicile's guests have none. This patch
relaxes the CHECK to "a guest SiteInstance implies a guest", and makes
a noopener window's SiteInstance for a guest only when the guest has a
guest SiteInstance. Content's guest path does the rest: it asks
WebViewGuest::CreateNewGuestWindow for the page and hands it back in
AddNewContents, which lists it as a browser window
(components/domicile/browser/web_view_guest.cc).

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
index 788df9d..f48a458 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
@@ -5768,9 +5768,14 @@ FrameTree* WebContentsImpl::CreateNewWindow(
       base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(features::kGuestViewMPArch)
           ? opener->GetOutermostMainFrame()->frame_tree()->is_guest()
           : IsGuest();
-  // While some guest types do not have a guest SiteInstance, the ones that
-  // don't all override WebContents creation above.
-  CHECK_EQ(source_site_instance->GetSecurityPrincipal().IsGuest(), is_guest);
+  // DOMICILE: a guest SiteInstance implies a guest, but a guest may have none.
+  // Domicile's <webview> guests share the default partition, so they keep the
+  // user's logins, and make new windows through
+  // BrowserPluginGuestDelegate::CreateNewGuestWindow below. See
+  // components/domicile/browser/web_view_guest.h.
+  const bool guest_site_instance =
+      source_site_instance->GetSecurityPrincipal().IsGuest();
+  CHECK(!guest_site_instance || is_guest);
 
   // We usually create the new window in the same BrowsingInstance (group of
   // script-related windows), by passing in the current SiteInstance.  However,
@@ -5778,7 +5783,9 @@ FrameTree* WebContentsImpl::CreateNewWindow(
   // SiteInstance is created in a new BrowsingInstance.
   scoped_refptr<SiteInstance> site_instance;
   if (params.opener_suppressed) {
-    if (is_guest) {
+    // DOMICILE: a guest without a guest SiteInstance has the default
+    // partition, which CreateForGuest refuses. See above.
+    if (guest_site_instance) {
       // For guests, noopener windows can be created in a new BrowsingInstance
       // as long as they preserve the guest's StoragePartition.
       site_instance =
